 #1 requires the new ADR to be 'listed in the ADR index', but the Scope section omits the two artifacts that inclusion actually requires: the per-ADR marker file docs/adr/.numbers/<NNNN> and the regenerated docs/adr/README.md. Both are machine-managed by scripts/gen_adr_index.py, and CI (gen_adr_index.py --check plus scripts/check_adr_numbers.py, which asserts the ADR-number/marker bijection) fails on drift. As written, landing only the ADR .md file leaves the index stale and the marker missing, so AC #1 is unsatisfiable and CI breaks.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff026deb3daa81a8b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope; Acceptance Criteria #1","norm_id":"n865cd25f7e22c1d6","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author adds only the ADR .md file; `make lint`/CI --check fails on stale index + missing .numbers marker","Reviewer applies AC #1 by reading the index and finds the new ADR absent"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Under Scope, add 'docs/adr/README.md (regenerated) and docs/adr/.numbers/<NNNN> (new marker), both produced by running scripts/gen_adr_index.py after assigning the next free ADR number', and replace the 00NN placeholder with the concrete assigned number.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the noise-band rule so it names a Pass-1 (Tier-2) noise baseline for finding-set deltas (e.g. a repeated-run finding-set stability floor on the fixed sample), or state explicitly that Tier-2 acceptance is judged only on downstream Tier-1/Tier-0 metrics against their bands.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the noise-band acceptance rule (a change is improving/regressing only outside the band from identical-material flips and the Tier-1 reproduction run)'","Plan tier table: 'Pass-1 criterion prompt → Tier 2 single-criterion (N=20) plus downstream; finder system prompt or chunking → Tier 2 full mode'","Epic 759e Tier-2 measures 'finding sets by norm_id/criterion' and its AC verifies only 'one baseline sample run' — no Tier-2 noise floor is defined, so a Pass-1 delta has no band to be judged against","ABSENCE: the doc/ADR as scoped names a Tier-1-derived band but no Pass-1/finding-set noise baseline"],"finding":"The noise-band acceptance rule is sourced only from identical-material flips and the Tier-1 reproduction run, but the plan makes Tier 2 (Pass-1) the required tier for the most common edit (a Pass-1 criterion prompt), and Tier 2 is scored by finding-set comparison (norm_id/criterion) rather than Tier-1's per-question agreement — so the documented band does not tell a contributor how to judge a Pass-1 finding-set delta as signal vs. noise.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2427e636e69bdd35","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — noise-band acceptance rule; tier-selection table (Pass-1 criterion prompt → Tier 2)","norm_id":"nb26960444b08d980","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A contributor edits a Pass-1 criterion prompt, runs Tier 2 (N=20), sees a finding-set Jaccard shift, and cannot tell from the protocol whether that shift exceeds finder run-to-run noise or is a real regression"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the ADR's noise-band section, define the band per tier: Tier-1/Tier-0 from identical-material flips + the Tier-1 reproduction run (as written), and Tier-2 from a repeated-sample finder finding-set stability run (or defer Tier-2 acceptance to its downstream Tier-1/Tier-0 deltas), so every required tier has a defined signal-vs-noise baseline.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the noise-band acceptance rule to name a Tier-2 (Pass-1) noise baseline — a finding-set stability floor (e.g. Jaccard / per-criterion gained-lost against the Tier-2 reproduction run, candidate_dir=None, temperature 0) — so proposals routed to Tier 2 single-criterion and full mode have a defined band, and state which statistic each tier's 'band' is computed over.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: the band is derived only 'from identical-material flips and the Tier-1 reproduction run' — Tier-0 and Tier-1 only.","Plan tier-selection table routes 'Pass-1 criterion prompt → Tier 2 single-criterion (N=20)' and 'finder system prompt or chunking → Tier 2 full mode' — i.e. the prompt-editing cases the guide primarily serves land in Tier 2.","Tool-verified: src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py emits finding_set_comparison() (whole-set Jaccard + per-criterion gained/lost) and verdict_flip_matrix() (newly_blocking/relieved) — a different output vocabulary from Tier-0's decision flips and Tier-1's per-question agreement.","Tool-verified: tier2 has a reproduction run (candidate_dir=None / 'current' via install_candidate_override) that would define a Tier-2 noise baseline (Jaccard finding-set stability at temperature 0), analogous to tier1.py's docstring calling its prompt_path=None run 'the Pass-2 noise floor at temperature 0' — yet the plan's noise-band rule names no Tier-2 baseline."],"finding":"The noise-band acceptance rule is defined only over Tier-0 'identical-material flips' and the Tier-1 reproduction run, but the tier-selection table routes Pass-1 criterion-prompt and finder-system-prompt/chunking changes to Tier 2, whose output is a finding-set Jaccard / verdict-flip signature with its own distinct reproduction-run baseline — so the rule as written cannot be applied to the Tier-2 outputs it is meant to gate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb9aa150bf60c9449","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach bullet 1 (\"the noise-band acceptance rule (a change is improving/regressing only outside the band from identical-material flips and the Tier-1 reproduction run)\") + Approach bullet 2 tier-selection table (Pass-1 criterion prompt → Tier 